  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Ice dams form when heat escapes from your attic, melts snow on the upper roof, and the water refreezes when it hits the colder eaves.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Long-Term Prevention (Fixing Attic Heat & Air Leaks)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To stop ice dams at the source, you need to keep the entire roof surface at a consistent, cold winter temperature:",
        "reference_indexes": [
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Improve Attic Insulation: Add insulation to your attic floor (aim for at least 8 to 9 inches or more) to stop warm air from escaping through the ceiling.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Seal Air Leaks: Seal bypasses around attic access doors, recessed lights, chimney chases, and plumbing stacks where warm air leaks into the attic.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ensure Proper Ventilation: Balance your eave (soffit) and ridge ventilation to flush out warm air and keep the roof deck cold.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Upgrade Roofing Material: Consider a steep-pitched metal roof, which helps shed snow faster and minimizes ice dam risks.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Short-Term & Active Solutions (Heat Cables and Panels)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "When structural changes aren't enough or you deal with heavy Wasatch Front snow and freeze-thaw cycles, mechanical and electrical systems can help:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Self-Regulating Heat Cables: Install commercial-grade heat trace cables (offered by local Utah providers like Wizard Rain Gutters and RGS Exteriors ) in a zig-zag pattern along the eaves, valleys, and inside gutters/downspouts. These automatically adjust their heat output based on the temperature.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Wizard Rain Gutters",
                "link": "https://www.wizardscreensandgutter.com/roof-ice-melt-systems/"
              },
              {
                "text": "RGS Exteriors",
                "link": "https://www.rgsexteriorsutah.com/gutters/heat-cable"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              6,
              7,
              8
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Heat Panels: Install metal edge panels with integrated self-regulating cables along the lower courses of the roof to create a clear drainage path.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              8,
              9
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Safe Snow Removal: Use a long-handled, wheeled roof rake from the ground to pull 3 to 4 feet of heavy snow off the edge of the roof after a storm\u2014never climb onto an icy roof.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              4,
              10
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Emergency Channeling: If an ice dam has already formed, fill a nylon stocking with calcium chloride (avoid harsh rock salt that damages concrete and plants) and lay it vertically across the ice dam to melt a drainage channel.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              10
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you need professional steam removal or heat cable setup in the Salt Lake City area, local licensed specialists like Olympus Roofing or Royal Dane Roofing handle winter ice remediation and damage repair.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Royal Dane Roofing",
            "link": "https://olympusroofing.com/ice-dams-winter-roof-leaks-salt-lake-city/"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          11
        ]
      }
    ],
